Appendix G

Stochastic Barrier Function: Additional Lemmas (Supplement to Chapter 15)

Lemma G.1 (Boundedness of sublevel sets). For any finite M, the set \{\theta \in \text{int}(\mathcal{C}_\epsilon) \mid V(\theta) \le M\} is compact.

Proof. V includes the KL divergence, which is coercive on \Theta, and the barrier B, which goes to infinity at the boundary. Hence, the sublevel set is closed and bounded away from the boundary, thus compact. ∎

Lemma G.2 (Sufficient condition for no overshoot). If the step size \alpha_k satisfies \alpha_k < \frac{2}{L + \mu/\delta_{\min}}, where \delta_{\min} is the minimum gap to the boundary across the sublevel set, then a single SGD step cannot cross the barrier.

Proof. The local Lipschitz constant of \nabla V is bounded by L + \mu/\delta_{\min} near the boundary; a standard descent lemma guarantees that the update stays inside the feasible region. ∎

These lemmas complete the rigorous justification of the barrier method for alignment under recursion.

